codex
Implemented a verified Track B generator based on the paper’s native \((L,2)\)-colouring objects.

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1404.6821/gen_1404_6821.py)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1404.6821/README.md)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1404.6821/selftest_report.json)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1404.6821/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1404.6821/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1404.6821/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Key results:

- Ships at `hard`: \(n=32\), \(2^{32}\) succinct vertices, 288 gates.
- Exact symbolic certificate: 30 characters, 2 atoms.
- All gated G1–G9 checks pass.
- Guessing: 0/200,000; exact probability \(2^{-32}\).
- Five adversarial attacks: 0/8 each.
- Reference GF(2) algorithm: 25,674 operations, 8/8 successes.
- Bare oracle shipping rung: 0/3 solved.
- Structural-hint arm: 0/3 solved.

The non-gating placebo diagnostic reached 0/2 before OpenRouter exhausted its account-wide key limit. The failed retries remain recorded rather than being miscounted as oracle failures.
